# POLICE-STYLE VIDEO SUMMARY
**Camera:** cam13_stream-13, CN Vidhyalaya P2 RLVD-2027
**Footage:** cam13_stream-13.mp4, 93 minutes (minutes 0–92)

---

## 1. SCENE
The camera overlooks an urban signalised junction with zebra crossings, stop lines and a left-side bus bay. The footage is night-time throughout; the road surface was wet for nearly the entire period, drying only at minute 92. Lighting is artificial street/intersection lighting consistent with CCTV night coverage.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE
Traffic flowed continuously and steadily across all 93 minutes with no gaps in flow. The dominant traffic was mixed urban: numerous motorcycles and scooters (frequently carrying two riders, some helmetless), many yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws (also blue, dark and yellow variants), and frequent cars — white hatchbacks were the most commonly recurring vehicle type (seen in nearly every minute of part 1), alongside silver, black, red, maroon and dark-grey cars, sedans, hatchbacks and SUVs.

Larger vehicles were a constant presence:
- **Buses:** minute 0 (orange/yellow), 3 (blue-and-white), 4 (blue), 6 (red body/white roof), 9 (white), 16 (white/blue coach at bus bay; green/white bus), 19–20 (blue and red), 24 (blue with red trim), 50 (blue with yellow roof), 60 (yellow/orange "Kabra Travels" coach; silver-grey), 67 (white Mercedes-Benz with blue accents), 68 (blue double-decker "Rajdoot"), 70 (yellow double-decker), 72 (large white coach; blue state-transit style city bus), 74 (two red city buses in convoy, 30–38s), 75 (blue), 78 (white SRTC-type), 81 (large white with blue lights), 84 (red "SAVAN"), 86 (white with blue accents), 89 (white/red), 90 (orange/brown).
- **Trucks:** minute 1 (large green/blue covered-load), 6 (green with blue cargo cover), 9 (green, parked near crosswalk), 19 (concrete mixer), 21 (yellow), 22 (orange/brown mini truck; white box truck), 68 (brown truck with "MOTOR" text), 70 (blue truck; white cargo truck).
- **Vans/SUVs:** white vans at minutes 4, 14, 15, 18, 20, 23; white box delivery van (15); white MPV/van, white goods tempos, small white box truck (part 3); white van with amber beacon lights, ambulance-type (71); white, black, silver, red and blue SUVs across many minutes.

Less common items: blue three-wheeler goods carrier and a rider with a large pale load (15); orange SUV turning left across the traffic path (21); white van with amber beacon/ambulance-type (71).

**People:** pedestrians were sparse. Crossings occurred at minutes 8 (man in black t-shirt and light trousers, ~13–18s), 10 (individual plus a group of three on scooters), 11, 13 (group on crosswalk), 14 (pedestrian in white clothing), 15, 20, 22, 55, 59, 63, 65, 71, 79 (cyclist in blue shirt and a walking pedestrian on the zebra), 84 (two people walking side-by-side through the intersection), and 91 (pedestrian on left crosswalk). Minute 24 noted no pedestrians. Small groups waited at stop lines (part 3). Motorcyclists clustered at crosswalks before dispersing on green signals (minutes 51, 70). Most riders wore dark clothing.

## 3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED

### CONFIRMED
- Toyota Innova, white — no plate visible — direction not stated — minute 17
- Hyundai Creta, silver — no plate visible — direction not stated — minute 17
- Mahindra Bolero, white — no plate visible — direction not stated — minute 17
- Tata Nexon, black, SUV — moving right — minute 82
- Mahindra Bolero, blue, SUV — moving right — minute 82
- Toyota Innova, white — direction not stated — minute 88
- Maruti Suzuki Swift, white — direction not stated — minute 88

(Note: minute 17 also lists a green "Tata Sumo" described as an auto-rickshaw; minute 88 lists the Swift as a "sedan" — both carried as stated in the observations.)

### PROBABLE (unconfirmed)
None identified. (No vehicle in the observations is explicitly marked "(unconfirmed)".)

## 4. REGISTRATIONS READ
None legible. The observations state no number plates were visible or legible at any point; there are no automatic reads to report, verified or otherwise.

## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS
- **Minute 92:** reckless-driving alert raised for vehicles moving through a red light (0s–3s), with a silver SUV and black SUV exiting right and a white bus entering from the left.
- **Minutes 15, 22–23:** traffic signal stuck on red for extended stretches.
- **Minute 21:** orange SUV turning left across the traffic path.
- **Minute 71:** white van with amber beacon lights, ambulance-type.
- **Minute 74:** two large red city buses passing in convoy (~30–38s).
- **Minute 92:** road surface noted as dry, the only dry point in the footage.

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION
No build-ups, queues or jams observed. Traffic flowed continuously throughout. The only stationary vehicles noted were a silver sedan and later a blue SUV stopping at the crosswalk (minute 2), a red sedan stopped at the stop line through minute 12, a green truck parked near the crosswalk (minute 9), a white car parked near the zebra crossing from ~30s (minute 6), a white hatchback parked near it (minute 23), and motorcyclists clustering at crosswalks before green signals (minutes 51, 70) — none of which constituted congestion.

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
- **Red-light jumping:** minute 92, 0s–3s — vehicles moving through a red light, triggering the reckless-driving alert (silver SUV and black SUV exiting right; white bus entering from left).
- **Helmetless riders:** noted among motorcyclists in part 1 (e.g., minute 3, two riders with pillion in light trousers; minutes 20 and 23, motorcycles with two riders) and in part 3 ("some riders without helmets").
- **Illegal parking:** a green truck parked near the crosswalk (minute 9); a white car parked near the zebra crossing from ~30s (minute 6); a white hatchback parked near it (minute 23).
- No wrong-way driving observed.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The scene was remarkably consistent across the full 93 minutes: a busy night-time junction with uninterrupted mixed urban traffic on a wet road. The dominant traffic throughout was two-wheelers, yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws and white cars/hatchbacks, with buses and trucks threading through regularly. Buses were a recurring feature in nearly every stretch of footage, with a notable cluster of distinctive branded/coach buses in part 3 (minutes 60–74: Kabra Travels, Mercedes-Benz, Rajdoot double-decker, yellow double-decker, state-transit style) and continued bus presence in part 4. Pedestrian activity was consistently sparse, limited to occasional individual crossings and small groups at stop lines, with a gap noted at minute 24. Traffic signals cycled normally for most of the period, with the exceptions of the stuck-red stretches at minutes 15 and 22–23. The footage was quietest in terms of incidents — almost nothing alert-worthy occurred until the very end, when the road dried (minute 92) and the single reckless-driving/red-light violation was recorded. The only other irregularities were signal malfunctions mid-footage and occasional parked/stopped vehicles near crossings. No collisions or dangerous pedestrian conflicts occurred at any point.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
There were no stretches of inactivity — traffic flowed in every minute. In terms of notable events, the footage was quiet throughout parts 1–3 (minutes 0–74), with only routine flow, normal signal cycling and sparse pedestrian crossings; part 4 (minutes 75–91) was similarly uneventful, with the sole incident of the entire recording occurring at minute 92.
