# CCTV REVIEW SUMMARY — cam25_33_dehgam, Dehgam

**Footage:** cam25_33_dehgam.mp4 — 631 minutes, commencing 04:20 on 08-08-2026. Recorded in continuous greyscale/IR low-light or early-morning monochrome conditions throughout.

---

## 1. SCENE

The camera overlooks a two-lane residential/junction street at Dehgam. The carriageway is wet with standing water and potholes for the first hours of footage, indicating recent or ongoing rain. Lighting is pre-dawn darkness initially, transitioning to overcast dawn light, then daylight around minute 283, and back to full night from approximately minute 293 onward; the remainder of the footage is infrared/greyscale night footage. Trees line the left verge, buildings and a side road appear on the right, and there is a background junction at the crest of the road. Vehicle colours in night footage are approximations only (e.g. "appearing white in IR").

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE

Traffic was light and free-flowing throughout the entire 631 minutes.

- **Motorcycles/scooters** were the dominant category, present in almost every active minute across the whole period, mostly single riders (generally helmetless where discernible), some with pillions, and occasional small groups (4–5 two-wheelers together at minute 158; 2–3 at minute 147; 4–5 motorcyclists riding together at minute 71).
- **Cars:** mostly white/light-coloured hatchbacks and compact SUVs, with occasional dark cars/SUVs/sedans (e.g. minutes 69, 174, 177, 189, 191, 196, 200, 202, 239, 246, 260, 262, 272, 273, 285, 292, 581).
- **Vans/light commercial:** white vans, mini-vans, ambulances-type box vans and light goods trucks at numerous points (minutes 2, 20, 26, 31, 35, 40, 41–43, 54, 66, 134, 146, 153, 163, 166, 167, 186, 189, 193, 196, 199, 202, 245, 245, 248–249, 250, 251, 267, 268, 269, 280, 283, 290, 504, 545, 548).
- **Trucks:** covered/canvas goods trucks, tippers and heavy lorries at minutes 18, 63, 108, 110, 117, 122, 129, 132, 133, 140, 142, 148, 165, 183, 231, 246, 247, 256, 272, 274, 281, 351 (heavy multi-axle at 361–362), 379 (two lorries), 381, 512, 535, 541, 542, 547, 552, 626.
- **Auto-rickshaws:** frequent, both moving and parked. Dark auto-rickshaws parked long-term at minutes 41–43, 52–76, 104–128, 129–139, 140–153, 165–178, 179–203, 230–251, 256–259.
- **Other:** tractors with trailers (minutes 131, 180, 196, 198, 199, 256, 286, and 153 — the latter carrying several seated people); cyclists (minutes 39, 67, 184, 232, 237, 278); buses (minute 201, light-bodied bus with dark grille, distant); a white taxi-style car with roof sign (minute 179).
- **Pedestrians:** sparse throughout, mostly individual crossings or verge-walking, in light or dark clothing; small groups included three adults with children (minute 56), three pedestrians (minute 69), two women in light traditional clothing (minute 269), and a man in white kurta-pyjama (minute 260). No pedestrians at all in night footage from minute 294 onward until minute 628 (a man in a light/white shirt and dark trousers on a light-coloured scooter).
- **Animals:** dogs crossed or rested on the road in minutes 4, 15, 41, 52, 65, 185, 237, 250, 251, 259, 260, 287, 313, 321, 324, 330, 331, 370; a bird/small animal at minute 258; a probable dog/cat at minutes 361–362; a probable animal at minute 569.

No vehicle makes, models or registration plates were legible at any point in the footage.

## 3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED

**CONFIRMED:**
None identified. The observations repeatedly state that no makes, models or number plates were identifiable in any minute.

**PROBABLE (unconfirmed):**
- Auto-rickshaw, Bajaj RE class (unconfirmed), entered and stopped in left-centre — minute 40.
- White compact hatchback, Swift/i10 class (unconfirmed), no plate, travelling away — minute 238.
- Dark scooter, possibly Activa-class (unconfirmed), parked at bottom-left kerb — minute 634.

## 4. REGISTRATIONS READ

None legible. No registration number was quoted or readable in any minute of the footage.

## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS

- **Minute 24:** a motorcycle with two riders stopped mid-road around 43s; the pillion (light/white top) dismounted, ran to the parked scooter at bottom-left, and both left the frame by ~48s. The most unusual interaction of the pre-dawn period.
- **Minute 120:** a white hatchback entered from the left, stopped in the right lane facing away, with a person in white standing at the driver's door from 17–32s.
- **Minutes 126–127:** a man in a white shirt and dark trousers walked around a stationary auto-rickshaw and stood mid-road facing away for the remainder of the clip; a second auto-rickshaw was active, reversing/relocating.
- **Minute 153:** a tractor with an open trailer carrying several seated people crossed left-to-right — flagged as the most unusual sighting of that period.
- **Minutes 165–178:** a seemingly unattended auto-rickshaw sat parked at bottom-right with an occupant/loitering person from minute 169 to the end.
- **Minutes 203, 626–627:** auto-rickshaws/motorcycles stopping mid-road or on the verge with people lingering beside them.
- **Minute 270:** a "child on a skateboard" gliding mid-road toward the right.
- **Minute 635:** a faint possible standing figure near buildings at mid-right, unconfirmed at available resolution.
- Nothing in the footage was assessed as criminal or requiring escalation; the above are the only events departing from routine passage.

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION

None observed. Traffic remained light and free-flowing throughout; the largest groups were the 4–5 riders at minutes 71 and 158 and pedestrians in threes at minutes 56 and 69, none amounting to a crowd or build-up.

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS

None observed. No wrong-way driving, red-light jumping or congestion-related violations were recorded. Note: many riders were helmetless where discernible (e.g. minute 50, right-lane rider closest to camera), but helmet status was frequently undeterminable in greyscale/IR footage; no formal violation is asserted. The long-stationary parked auto-rickshaws (minutes 41–43, 52–76, 104–128, 165–203, 230–251) occupied the carriageway/verge but their parking status is not confirmed as illegal.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY

The scene follows a clear day-cycle. The pre-dawn hours (minutes 1–75, 04:20–~05:35) were very quiet: motorcycles with single riders, a handful of vans and cars, and the first appearance of the long-parked dark auto-rickshaw that became a constant fixture. From minutes 76–203 (dawn into ~07:43) activity rose slightly but remained light, with the auto-rickshaw(s) parked at the junction for extended stretches, a recurring pattern of people approaching, interacting with, and boarding or loading them. Mid-morning through daylight (minutes ~230–293) was the busiest phase — a steady but still light flow of motorcycles, white hatchbacks, vans, goods trucks and tractors, with goods loading beside parked autos (minutes 233–236) and the daylight-to-night transition at minute 293. From minute 294 to the end of the footage (minute 640), the scene reverted to near-total night-time inactivity: only sparse headlight-only passages by two-wheelers, cars and occasional heavy trucks, several long fully-static stretches, and a dark scooter parked unattended at bottom-left from minute 631 onward. Throughout, the wet/potholed carriageway persisted as an environmental constant, and the footage never yielded a legible plate or identifiable make.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS

Fully static or near-static minutes/stretches included:
- Minutes 3, 5–6, 10–12, 19, 21–23, 28–30, 34, 38, 44–45, 51, and various isolated minutes pre-dawn.
- Minutes 296, 299, 303–306, 308 (completely static night).
- Minutes 314, 317, 320, 323, 332, 334 (fully static).
- Minutes 360, 367, 368, 372, 374–377, 382–383 (completely static).
- Minutes 439–443 (no activity) and 446–459 (entirely static, 14 consecutive minutes).
- Minutes 485–491, 495–496, 498–501, 505–506 (mostly static).
- Minutes 510–534 (almost entirely static; only minutes 511, 512 and 533 showed movement).
- Minutes 550, 553–559, and most of minutes 560–584 (only 561, 566, 567, 569, 576, 581 active).
- Minutes 585–596, 599, 601–602, 604, 606–609 (static).
- Minutes 610–615, 617–619, 621–623, 625, 629–630, 632, 636–640 (static; minutes 636–640 entirely empty).

**End of summary.**
