VIDEO SUMMARY — cam03_03_O.N.G.C._Office (O.N.G.C. Office)
==============================================================================
**POLICE CCTV SUMMARY — cam03_03_O.N.G.C._Office (BS-103_B1), O.N.G.C. Office**
Footage covered: 686 minutes, 21:00 on 13-06-2026 through ~09:00 on 14-06-2026 (daytime portions not fully described in the observations).

---

**1. SCENE**

The camera overlooks a roadside carriageway at the O.N.G.C. Office, with a bus shelter on the left, a rubble verge, and a right-side railing/barrier beyond which vehicles sometimes park. Night footage (21:00 to ~05:15) was captured largely in infrared/monochrome, severely degraded by headlight glare, rain, wet reflective roads, fog/haze, lens moisture, pixelation and at times full digital corruption. From dawn onward (approx. minutes 578–718, roughly 08:20–09:00 on 14-06-2026) footage was colour daylight. Weather was persistently wet through the night — recent rain from about minute 30, heavy rain at many later points (e.g. minutes 164, 167–168, 215, 222, 447–448, 456–458, 476 onward) — clearing to a busy Sunday morning by the end of the coverage.

---

**2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE**

Traffic throughout the night was light, sparse and free-flowing, dominated by two-wheelers (motorcycles and scooters, frequently with pillion riders) seen mostly as headlight glare. Cars appeared regularly in white/light and dark colourways; auto-rickshaws (green-and-yellow, and yellow-and-white/black) recurred throughout; buses and heavy trucks appeared intermittently; occasional cyclists, vans and goods vehicles were noted. From the morning period (minutes 578–718) traffic increased to steady mixed flow: numerous motorcycles/scooters with pillions, many green-and-yellow auto-rickshaws, white vans, cars of various colours (white, black, silver, grey, red, dark grey SUVs and hatchbacks, a silver taxi sedan with roof sign), multiple city buses (GSRTC blue-and-white, red city buses, blue/orange livery, a teal "JODHPUR" coach, a red AMTC city bus), a light-cream mini goods truck, a municipal tipper, and a produce truck.

Pedestrians were very rare overnight — the vast majority of minutes show none at all — with occasional figures at or near the bus shelter (frequently in light/white shirts) and two notable street incidents involving people handling carts/objects (minutes 18, 68–69). From morning onward pedestrians remained sparse but more regular (small groups, individuals in white shirts, saffron/orange traditional attire, a woman with orange/saffron dupatta, and a large footpath group in minute 696).

Counted totals are not possible across most of the night due to degradation; the only precise counts stated: minute 600 had five two-wheelers; minute 231 had three two-wheelers; minute 355 had two two-wheelers plus a third vehicle.

One animal was recorded: a pale/white stray dog foraging near the shelter (minutes 367, 371, 372), with dog-like/dog-sized shapes on the carriageway at minutes 457 and 466.

---

**3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED**

**CONFIRMED:**
- Maruti Suzuki Dzire, white, plate GJ 18 BY 7580, entered top of frame and remained stationary in the carriageway facing away from camera, minute 175 (through end of that clip).

All other vehicles: only class and colour guesses; no other make/model confirmed.

**PROBABLE (unconfirmed):**
- Green-and-white three-wheeled goods carrier (Bajaj Maxima/loading-auto class), minute 711 (unconfirmed), entering toward camera ~55s.
- Probable Creta/Seltos/Harrier-class red SUV, minute 587 (class-level guess; not a confirmed make/model).

---

**4. REGISTRATIONS READ**

- GJ 18 BY 7580 — minute 175, white Maruti Suzuki Dzire. This is a single automatic read, not verified against any registry.

No other registration plate was legible at any point in the footage.

---

**5. NOTABLE EVENTS**

- **Minute 23 (~50s):** unexplained bright flame/orange fire appearing mid-carriageway, receding out of view by ~55s. Cause unexplained.
- **Minutes 68–69 (~47s and 0–5s):** a person in light-coloured clothing pushing/manoeuvring a three-wheeled cart in the middle of the road, then the same or similar person handling a table/stand-like object near the kerb before disappearing — flagged in the observations as the most unusual events of that sequence.
- **Minute 175–176:** a white Maruti Suzuki Dzire (GJ 18 BY 7580) stopped stationary in the carriageway; in minute 176 a white sedan with taxi-style yellow commercial plate sat with brake lights on while a man in dark clothing walked from rubble on the left to its driver side (~5–17s) before disappearing.
- **Minute 714 (~20s):** a person in light blue clothing with a white/light scooter appeared at bottom right apparently on or near the ground, possibly having fallen, getting up ~25–27s.
- **Minute 237 (~25–37s):** a person in light/reflective clothing ran across the roadway.
- **Minute 366:** a motorcycle with bright headlamp stood at bottom-right with a person in light clothing walking beside/behind it, appearing to push or attend to it, both exiting by ~12s.
- **Minutes 126 (0–10s), 138 (~35s), 356, 418, 374–375/377/380–381, 475, 229–230, 233/239/246/257, 259–277 (intermittent):** various stationary vehicles — a red bus at the left shelter (126); a heavy vehicle apparently slowing/stopping at the far end (138); a white bus/coach stationary at top-right (356); a vehicle parked/stationary behind the right railing (418, also 374/375/377/380/381 and a distant stationary vehicle in 475); distant stationary lit vehicles (229–230, recurring faint stationary light 233–257 and 259–277).
- Severe image corruption/glitching at minutes 0, 7, 37, 183, 197 (unproces sable), 582–586, 687, 697, and first ~35s of 715; heavy pixelation at 81, 87, 96, 108, 149; brief colour/mode switches at 27, 44, 46.

---

**6. CROWD AND CONGESTION**

No traffic queues or jams were observed at any point; all night traffic was free-flowing. Pedestrian build-ups were minimal: a small roadside cluster including someone in pink (minute 584); a group of 2–3 pedestrians with a parked two-wheeler at bottom-right from ~50s (minute 603); three pedestrians in saffron/orange traditional attire (minute 694); and a large group on the footpath from ~37s (minute 696). Otherwise no crowd formation of note.

---

**7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS**

- **Helmetless riders:** minute 597 (scooter with pillion in pink, no helmets); minutes 715–716 (helmetless rider in green on dark scooter; helmetless rider on red scooter).
- **Possible obstruction/stationary vehicle in carriageway:** minute 175, white Maruti Suzuki Dzire (GJ 18 BY 7580) stopped stationary in the carriageway; minute 176, white taxi-style sedan stationary with brake lights on.
- No wrong-way driving or red-light running observed.

---

**8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY**

The coverage shows a classic overnight decay of traffic from a busy Saturday evening into a deserted pre-dawn, followed by a Sunday morning build-up. From 21:00 to roughly 22:40 (parts 1–5), traffic was light but constant — two-wheelers, cars, auto-rickshaws and occasional buses/trucks on wet roads under deteriorating weather (recent rain from ~minute 30, fog at minute 31). From ~22:40 through 01:50 (parts 6–11), activity thinned further, dominated by headlight-only sightings with pedestrians almost absent; recurrent stationary lights at the top-right edge and behind the right railing appear throughout this stretch. The deepest quiet runs from ~00:53 to ~05:15 (parts 10–19): deserted wet road, only sporadic two-wheelers and cars, animals instead of people (dog, minutes 367–372, 457, 466), and weather repeatedly reducing footage to light streaks. From ~05:15 onward traffic gradually returned, and by the morning period (minutes 578–718, ~08:20–09:00 Sunday) the scene was at its busiest: steady mixed flow of two-wheelers (many with pillions, several carrying two or even three riders), auto-rickshaws, public-service buses, vans and goods vehicles, with daylight colour footage finally allowing colour and body-type detail. Recurring elements across the whole period: the bus shelter with occasional brief occupants (usually in light/white clothing), green-and-yellow auto-rickshaws, and persistent rain/glare/pixelation that made most night identifications impossible.

---

**9. QUIET PERIODS**

- Minute 222: entirely traffic-free (heavy rain).
- Minute 436: no moving vehicle entered the frame; only static distant lights.
- Minutes 233–258 (approx. 00:53–01:18): deserted road, very sparse traffic.
- Minutes 259–290 (01:19–01:50): light unidentifiable glare only, no confirmed pedestrians.
- Minutes 342–366: "almost entirely deserted"; minutes 356 and 367–372 essentially empty except a stationary bus and a stray dog.
- Minutes 418–469 (approx. 03:58–05:15): sparse pre-dawn traffic, near-whiteouts in 447–448 and 456–458; minutes 456, 458, 460, 466, 469 showed only distant lights.
- Minutes 470–495 (04:50–05:15): consistently very light traffic throughout.
- Minute 707: empty for the first ~15s.
- Isolated empty/degraded minutes: 7, 37, 108, 183, 197, 583 (corruption/pixelation preventing observation).
