# POLICE SUMMARY — CCTV cam31_stream-31 (GDM-Rambaugh/Rambagh PTZ2)

**Location:** Hiralal Parakh Circle roundabout junction
**Footage reviewed:** ~643 minutes, 21:00 on 08-08-2026 to approx. 08:15 on 09-08-2026

---

## 1. SCENE

The camera overlooks Hiralal Parakh Circle, a multi-directional roundabout junction with lit shopfronts on the left, market stalls on the right, and a central monument/island. The footage begins after dark (21:00) in full night conditions, runs through the overnight hours into pre-dawn darkness, and ends in daylight by approximately minute 549 (~06:00–06:30 onward). Recurring problems: glare and headlight flare at night, rear-only vehicle angles, severe compression artefacts (minutes 73, 97, 104, 169, 170, 185, 234), frame corruption at the start of minutes 3 and 19, and a frame jump in minute 227. Numerous minutes returned no processable frames at all (null records) and cannot be read as evidence the scene was empty.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE

- **Evening peak (minutes 0–52, 21:00–21:50):** heavy multi-directional traffic, roughly 15–40 vehicles per minute — numerous motorcycles/scooters (many two-up, predominantly helmetless), cars in white, black, silver, grey, red, maroon, gold/brown and one blue, auto-rickshaws (green-yellow and black-yellow), goods trucks, tankers, and multiple buses (SADABAHAR coach, Amul delivery truck, PCBL staff bus, RISHABH TRAVELS and RISHABH SMART MOBILITY coaches, JSN intercity coach).
- **Late evening (minutes 53–152):** steady 10–30 cars and 15–30 two-wheelers per readable minute; delivery riders with yellow boxes (mins 67–68, 110, 218); tippers, tractors with trailers, and a "gokul" coach (146). From minute 138 a police/emergency presence appeared and persisted.
- **Overnight (minutes 153–463):** progressive decline to light, sparse traffic — isolated motorcycles, dark and white cars, occasional three-wheelers, an ambulance (382), stray dogs and cows, with extended completely static stretches.
- **Dawn/morning (minutes 540–718):** traffic rebuilt — white buses, trucks (KATARIA/BALAJI WAFERS container truck at 598), tippers, tractors, a backhoe loader (706), heavy two-wheeler traffic (8–20 at a time), and 10–15 pedestrians during busy minutes (684, 689, 698).
- **Pedestrians:** small groups loitering near left shops and right stalls throughout the evening; individual crossings at mins 25, 28, 50, 77, 143, 216, 252; no pedestrians at all during the overnight stretch (mins 385–463); groups of 10–15 during morning peaks.

## 3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED

### CONFIRMED
- Hyundai i20, white, plate partly legible GJ-?-ZB-8460, stationary bottom-left, minute 3.
- Tata Nexon/Altroz-class vehicle with "Altroz" tailgate badging, white, plate not legible, moving away bottom-left, minute 139.
- Maruti Suzuki Swift, white, minute 140.
- Maruti Suzuki Wagon R, white, minute 140.
- Maruti Suzuki sedan (S-cross/Dzire-type grille badge), white, plate not legible, minute 144.
- Mercedes-Benz coach bus, white, rear view, plate not legible, moving off left, minute 666.
- Toyota Innova-type MPV, silver/champagne, plate GJ12AK7020, stationary facing camera near-right, minute 707 (confirmed by body shape and grille badge).
- White Hyundai SUV (make badge visible on bonnet; model unidentified), approaching and turning, minute 31.

### PROBABLE (unconfirmed)
- White minibus/Force Traveller-type (unconfirmed), minute 0.
- White Mahindra Bolero-class hard-top pickup, minute 4.
- White Creta/Seltos-class SUV (unconfirmed), parked lower-left, minutes 10, 50, 55 and 402–403.
- White Fortuner/Scorpio-class SUV with rear-mounted spare wheel (unconfirmed), minute 43.
- Dark maroon compact sedan (probable), minute 64.
- White Ertiga-class MPV (probable), minute 64.
- Mahindra-class white boxy 4x4 utility vehicle (confirmed silhouette only), minute 66.
- White boxy SUV of Bolero/Sumo class (unconfirmed), minute 218.
- White SUV of Vitara Brezza/Sonet class (unconfirmed), minute 442.
- White SUV/MPV of Ertiga/XL6 class (unconfirmed), minute 465.
- Light-coloured mini goods carrier/tempo of Bolero Maxx class (unconfirmed), minute 465.
- White hatchback of i10/WagonR class (unconfirmed), minute 489.

## 4. REGISTRATIONS READ

- GJ-?-ZB-8460 (partial, one character unreadable) — minute 3, white Hyundai i20. Single automatic read, not verified against any registry.
- GJ12CP5548 — minute 682, white van with roof luggage rack. Single automatic read, not verified against any registry.
- GJ 12 DG 1739 — minute 695, white hatchback. Single automatic read, not verified against any registry.
- GJ12AK7020 — minute 707, silver/champagne Toyota Innova-type MPV. Single automatic read, not verified against any registry.
- A yellow plate on the PCBL staff bus (minute 39) was partially legible only; no characters recorded.

## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS

- Minute 2: ambulance passed through the junction.
- Minute 3 and 19: severe frame corruption at start of each minute (usable from ~8s and ~20s).
- Minute 16: rider standing on the cargo deck of a moving open goods truck.
- Minutes 17–18: blue-and-white "Amul / Real Milk Ice Cream / ISHA SALES" delivery truck parked bottom-left.
- Minute 20: hand-drawn cart on the carriageway.
- Minute 24: red-cab tanker truck crossing leftward.
- Minute 39: white "PCBL / STAFF BUS / Rishabh's" staff bus entered from the right.
- Minute 73: severe compression artefacts (~12–33s).
- Minute 97: severe picture corruption/vertical striping (~12–14s, recovered by ~32s).
- Minutes 138–207: persistent police/emergency presence — white police SUV with light bar (138), then a white police/ambulance-type van with flashing red/blue lights parked on the left with 4–6 uniformed personnel, growing to ~8–12 by minutes 176–178; two white vans/ambulances at the left kerb from minute 202; white car with red beacon stationary (144). Appears to be a checkpoint or vehicle stop; no outcome observed.
- Minute 160: white ambulance-type box van with beacons active moved away toward the circle.
- Minutes 104, 169–170, 185, 227, 234: compression artefacts, colour distortion, signal glitching or frame jump.
- Minute 235, 238, 259, 225: fully static minutes with no activity.
- Minute 245: feed failed entirely — no frames received.
- Minute 382: white ambulance-type van with blue stripe, "AMBULANCE" and "108" markings in the lower-left foreground, gone by ~20s.
- Minutes 408–412: white cow standing at bottom right, persisting across minutes.
- Minute 548: large blue-tarpaulin-covered goods truck in the foreground.
- Minute 598: large white/red "KATARIA" / "BALAJI WAFERS" container truck with blue tarpaulin occupied the centre of the junction.
- Minutes 619–625: unusual — a large herd of over 100 goats and sheep filled the right side of the junction, persisting into minute 625.
- Minute 684–689: large blue tarpaulin-covered truck parked in the near foreground, partially blocking the lower frame.
- Null/unreadable minutes throughout (e.g. 53, 58, 59, 61, 63, 70, 75, 76, 79, 82, 83, 87, 88, 89, 94, 103, 106, 111, 116, 118, 123, 128, 131, 133, 135–137, 153, 245, 259, 545–546) — these must not be read as evidence the scene was empty and should be re-run.

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION

No traffic jams, queues or crowd build-ups were observed at any point, despite heavy evening volumes. Pedestrian groups were small (2–6 near stalls/shops; 5–8 at minute 223; 10–15 at minutes 684, 689, 698). The only sustained gathering was the group of 4–12 people around the parked police/ambulance vehicles at minutes 138–207, apparently a checkpoint or vehicle stop.

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS

- Helmetless riders: noted throughout the footage — predominantly helmetless two-wheeler riders with 10–30 two-wheelers per minute during the evening peak (mins 25–52), two possible helmetless riders (minute 371), helmetless rider in reddish shirt (minute 503), two-up motorcycle without helmets (minute 492), and "most riders helmetless" during morning minutes 665–700. No specific rider is individually identified.
- No wrong-way driving, red-light jumping or illegal parking was observed in any readable clip.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY

The period shows a classic overnight decay curve. The junction was busiest between 21:00 and ~22:30 (minutes 0–~90), carrying continuous heavy mixed traffic of 15–40 vehicles per minute dominated by two-wheelers, with frequent bus movements. From ~22:30 to midnight traffic thinned to light-to-moderate flows, coinciding with the arrival of a police/ambulance presence on the left (minute 138 onward) that remained in place for over an hour. After midnight (minutes 206 onward) traffic became sparse — isolated motorcycles, occasional cars and three-wheelers — reaching its quietest between roughly 02:25 and 06:25, when most minutes were entirely static and only scattered single vehicles and animals moved through the junction. Activity resumed with dawn around minutes 540–549 and built through the morning: the KATARIA container truck at minute 598, the goat herd at minutes 619–625, and increasingly busy mixed traffic from minute 657 onward, peaking around minutes 684–698 with 15–20 two-wheelers and 10–15 pedestrians per minute. Recurring elements across the whole period: parked goods trucks/tempi on the left roadside, stray dogs (and occasionally cows) on the carriageway, delivery riders with yellow boxes, and persistent headlight glare and camera artefacts that prevented most vehicle identifications.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS

- Minutes 128–137: multiple unreadable/null minutes (128, 131, 133, 135–137); no conclusions drawable.
- Minutes 153–589 (overnight): progressively quieter, with extensive fully static stretches — notably minutes 443–445, 448–451, 470–471, 473, 476, 478, 480–483, 486–488, 490–491, 493, 495, 497–499, 502, 504–507, 509–512, 545–546, 550–564, 565–570 and 572–589.
- Minutes 356–383: most minutes static with no activity.
- Minutes 640–664: static in nearly every minute except 657 and 662.
- Minutes 669–700: many null minutes (669, 670, 683, 685–688, 690–693, 696, 697, 700).
- Minutes 701–718: several minutes with no detectable activity (702, 705, 708, 709, 714, 716, 718).
- Minute 225: recorded no activity at all; minutes 235, 238, 259 completely static; minute 245 no frames received.

All null/unreadable minutes listed above should be re-processed before any conclusion is drawn about those periods.
