# POLICE SUMMARY – CCTV cam02_02_Janpath ("Janpath T CSITMS-10_PTZ2")

**Coverage:** ~693 minutes (minutes 0–719), 13-06-2026 ~21:00 to 14-06-2026 morning, Janpath T-junction.

---

## 1. SCENE

The camera overlooks the Janpath T-junction, a signal-controlled intersection with a central median/island, zebra crossings, a Gujarat Police barricade at the right of the crossing, and footpaths either side. The footage begins in darkness (colour with heavy headlight glare), transitions to greyscale/IR night mode through the small hours, with dawn breaking around minute 527 (colour from ~10s in) and overcast daylight thereafter. The road surface was wet and reflective for almost the entire period, consistent with recent or light rain (visible rain streaks at minute 360; damp/drying by minutes 703–704). Night footage was persistently degraded by glare, IR bloom and motion blur; no registration plates were legible at any point.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE

Traffic was continuous and free-flowing throughout, varying only in volume. Typical composition per minute:

- **Two-wheelers:** the dominant mode throughout — roughly 8–25 motorcycles/scooters per minute, often carrying pillions, occasionally two or three occupants on one machine (mins 207, 286, 541, 545, 570, 578, 583, 611, 613, 652, 688, 715, 716). Riders mostly in dark clothing; helmet use mixed and often unverifiable.
- **Cars:** roughly 6–20 per minute, predominantly white, plus black, silver/grey, dark grey, maroon/dark red, occasional red, dark blue, pink (min 122) and pale pink/lavender (min 18) examples — hatchbacks, sedans, SUVs, MPVs and vans.
- **Auto-rickshaws:** 2–12 per minute, predominantly green-and-yellow CNG autos, plus dark, white-canopied and goods/loader three-wheelers.
