# POLICE SUMMARY — CCTV cam01_01_Chiman_bhai_Bridge (CSITMS-32_PTZ2), Chiman bhai Bridge
Footage reviewed: 663 minutes, from 21:00 on 13-06-2026 through approx. 08:57 on 14-06-2026.

## 1. SCENE
The camera overlooks the Chiman bhai Bridge junction: a multi-lane road with two-way traffic, a left service road/verge containing an auto-rickshaw stand, bus stop ("CHITRA" sign), stalls and an elevated viaduct (a train was visible crossing it at minutes 518 and 528). The footage spans night (21:00 onwards), the full overnight period, and ends in Sunday-morning daylight (08:57). Road surface was damp/reflective for most of the period, consistent with recent rain (described as dry at minute 186 and around minute 142). Heavy oncoming headlight glare and distance repeatedly degraded detail; no number plates were readable at any point.

## 2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE
Traffic was continuous and free-flowing in both directions throughout all 663 minutes. Dominant vehicle types:
- **Auto-rickshaws:** numerous yellow-and-green (some yellow/black, yellow/cream, white/green, green/white), roughly 4–20 visible per minute; a rank of 4–10 was parked/queued on the left verge/forecourt in virtually every minute, with individuals periodically pulling out.
- **Motorcycles/scooters:** roughly 4–25 per minute depending on hour; riders mostly in white/light or dark clothing; several appeared helmetless (e.g. minutes 0, 527, 557, 653).
- **Cars:** predominantly white sedans, hatchbacks, SUVs and MPVs, plus frequent dark/black, silver/grey, red, maroon and occasional light-blue or orange vehicles. A dark vintage-style car (minute 644) and an orange/amber taxi (minute 246) were noted.
